# Frontend Rules (Next.js 16)

**Read first:** `frontend/AGENTS.md` and `frontend/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — Next.js 16 differs from older versions.

## Stack

Next.js 16.2 · React 19 · TypeScript · Tailwind v4 · shadcn (`base-nova`) · `@base-ui/react` · `@supabase/ssr` · Zod

## Routing

| Group | Path | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| `(auth)` | `src/app/(auth)/` | login, signup, forgot-password |
| `(app)` | `src/app/(app)/` | authed shell (sidebar, home, forms) |
| Public | `src/app/f/[slug]/` | respondent form — slug only, no internal id |
| Callback | `src/app/auth/callback/route.ts` | Supabase code exchange |

## Session / auth

- **Gate:** `src/proxy.ts` exports `proxy` (not `middleware.ts`).
- **Refresh:** `src/lib/supabase/proxy.ts` → `updateSession`.
- **Public paths:** `/`, `/login`, `/signup`, `/forgot-password`, `/auth/callback`, `/f/*`, `_next/*`.
- **Mutations:** Server Actions in `src/app/(auth)/actions.ts` only (`signIn`, `signUp`, `signOut`, `requestPasswordReset`).

## Supabase clients

| Context | Helper |
|---------|--------|
| Client Components | `createSupabaseBrowserClient()` |
| Server Components, actions, routes | `await createSupabaseServerClient()` |

Never use service role in client bundles. Server-only secrets stay in server components/actions.

## UI components

- Primitives in `src/components/ui/` use Base UI `render={...}` slot pattern — match when adding components.
- Icons: `lucide-react`.
- Toasts: `sonner` where used.

## Forms domain

- Load published definitions via `public_forms` (see `src/lib/data/public-form.ts`).
- Validate answers with `src/lib/public-form/validate-answers.ts`; keys = field `id` (`f_*`).
- Publish: set `public_slug` with `nanoid(12)` when status → `published`.
- Preserve `needs_review` on fields when saving editor state.

## Backend API calls

Sketch generation hits FastAPI with `Authorization: Bearer <session JWT>`:

```ts
POST {API}/api/v1/forms/generate
{ storage_path, form_id? }
```

Storage uploads: `sketches/{userId}/{formId or filename}.{ext}`.

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev | build | start | lint
```

No `test` script — ask before adding.

